      "side": 1,
      "message": "That makes a lot of sense. My initial implementation of the change checker [1] back in 2019 was considering up-to-date if the target SHA1 was *exactly* the value of the NoteDb\u0027s `/meta` ref. That is the reason why the indexing was happening *unconditionally* even if the change wasn\u0027t up-to-date for managing the situation where the `/meta` was fast-moving and the target `/meta` was mostly more advanced.\n\nNow that we simply check for the `/meta` existence on the repository, it makes sense to remove the unconditional indexing.\n\n[1] https://gerrit-review.googlesource.com/c/plugins/high-availability/+/183251/40/src/main/java/com/ericsson/gerrit/plugins/highavailability/index/ChangeCheckerImpl.java",
